.TH LLITE.PCC_ATTACH_THREAD_MAX 4 2026-08-26 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
llite.pcc_attach_thread_max \- limit number of PCC copy threads per mount
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param llite." FSNAME *.pcc_attach_thread_max
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param llite." FSNAME *.pcc_attach_thread_max= THREAD_COUNT
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per local filesystem mountpoint.
.TP
.B Config
.br
.B pcc_attach_thread_max
is always present for client mountpoints.
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB pcc_attach_thread_max= 1024
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
.RB pcc_attach_thread_max= 1
.br
.RB pcc_attach_thread_max= 16384
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Persistent Client Cache file attach process starts background file
copy threads when a cache-eligible file is accessed to perform the
.BR lfs-pcc-attach (1)
operation.  The specified
.I THREAD_COUNT
is the maximum number of background threads started on each mountpoint.
The default
.B 1024
limit is expected to be sufficient for most uses, but is tunable up or down.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B llite.*.pcc_attach_thread_max
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Permanently limit the number of background copy threads per mountpoint to 16:
.RB "mgs# " "lctl set_param -P llite.*.pcc_attach_thread_max=16"
.EE
.PP
Limit the number of background copy threads to 32 for the
.B testfs
filesystem on the local
.BR client :
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param llite.testfs-*.enable_setstripe_gid=32"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B llite.pcc_attach_thread_max
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.57-xx
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-pcc-attach (1),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
